<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>King Charles warns of 'existential danger' of AI falling into wrong hands</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:58:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o--87edd459c4d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The comments were made at a summit in Scotland with participants from AI giants including Nvidia, OpenAI and Anthropic.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why are there concerns AI could threaten humanity, and how real are they?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:18:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno--8128fa4f3ef2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Existential fears about AI have once again reared their head - here's what you need to know.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uncontrolled AI could lead to 'silicon species' rivalling humans, warns Microsoft</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n07ypqz8kzo#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:22:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n07ypqz8kzo--4a87dc1c7397.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n07ypqz8kzo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Mustafa Suleyman says he believes rival AI firm Anthropic is in effect teaching Claude it "may be conscious".</summary></entry><entry><title>Snapchat open to putting time limits on teens, boss tells BBC</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3wjz3edd10o#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3wjz3edd10o--69d773778745.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3wjz3edd10o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Evan Spiegel says it would be "an important step forward for the industry" in an interview with the BBC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Would you buy branded clothing from your favourite tech firm?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgqd9zkkvlyo#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:18:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgqd9zkkvlyo--14bb7b514bbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgqd9zkkvlyo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia, OpenAI and Anthropic are all now selling their own limited edition fashion lines.</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI boss says world 'right to be afraid' but should trust AI firms</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:02:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o--4686332c8f93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Sam Altman and other tech CEOs say there are incentives to limit advancements in AI, as fears grow over the threats it poses to humanity.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI app ads promoting 'objectification of women' banned by watchdog</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T23:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o--3f8309803edf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The ad regulator said it had "zero-tolerance" for ads promoting AI tools that could sexualise or objectify women.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pubs in England and Wales to allow digital ID apps to prove age</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gl6j53w19o#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T23:07:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gl6j53w19o--5a4264a30fd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gl6j53w19o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">New rules introduced on Tuesday mean establishments will be able to accept digital ID apps alongside physical documents.</summary></entry><entry><title>Valve's Steam Frame is excellent - but at over £1,000 is VR still too expensive?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8m1113ym1o#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:05:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8m1113ym1o--e3780432d3ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8m1113ym1o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC's Tom Gerken is hands-on with the latest virtual reality headset.</summary></entry><entry><title>What is AI, how does it work and why are some people concerned about it?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2l799gxjjpo#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T16:09:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2l799gxjjpo--7bb18b050612.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2l799gxjjpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">AI is transforming modern life, but not without worry for some that it may be abused or have an adverse environmental impact.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump downplays warnings of AI risks, citing rivalry with China</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c7v48vp31mdo#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:49:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c7v48vp31mdo--405af91616a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c7v48vp31mdo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The US president said "negative forces" were airing concerns about "things that won't happen".</summary></entry><entry><title>Questions mount over what an AI 'slowdown' would look like</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzp47py48o#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:20:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzp47py48o--6e6573f8c1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzp47py48o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">While pacing AI development might sound like a quick fix, it is far from an easy solution.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI staff 'genuinely frightened' for humanity's future, ex-Anthropic researcher tells BBC</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1kx0gyje9wo#0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T14:53:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1kx0gyje9wo--e2bc2fc4f2ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1kx0gyje9wo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">It comes as the AI firm's boss has called for the technology's development to be slowed down, citing "serious" risks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyf#2</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyf--0cfb3dcdb81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyf?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">What should children learn in a world transformed by artificial intelligence?</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyd#2</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T20:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyd--0bf850c7b0e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyd?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Scammers demand money from Instagram users over fake copyright claims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyc#2</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T20:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyc--aac336945946.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyc?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">AI can only communicate in languages that it's been trained on.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc